(27) He has also made reference to
Veettil Chandanathil Mukkayi v. Parambil Puthavumma, (S
) where it was observed that the power of a court to direct restitution was inherent in the court of justice was under a duty to repair the injury done to a party by its act. It was observed that the principle of restitution was not confined to provisions of section 144, C. P. C.
